---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'inquiries', label: 'Project inquiries' },
  { id: 'email', label: 'Email' },
  { id: 'spam', label: 'Spam protection' },
  { id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics' },
  { id: 'hosting', label: 'Hosting and logs' },
  { id: 'booking', label: 'Booking a call' },
  { id: 'processors', label: 'Who processes data' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How IsmailApps handles personal data on ismailapps.com: project inquiries, email, spam protection, cookieless analytics and booking calls."
  updated="8 November 2026"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data this website processes, why, and for how long. We collect as little as we
    can: the details you choose to send us in a project inquiry, and the technical minimum needed to run the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    IsmailApps is the name under which {site.founder.legalName} offers software product services. It is not a registered
    company yet. The person responsible for your data (the controller) is:
  </p>
  <address>
    {site.founder.legalName}<br />
    {site.founder.postalAddress}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </address>
  <p>We work from Pakistan, so the information you send us is also accessed from there.</p>

  <h2 id="inquiries">Project inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the form on <a href="/contact">Start a project</a>, we receive your name, email address, company or
    product name (optional), what you need, where your product is today, your budget range and timeline, your
    description, and an optional link.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Why:</strong> to reply to you and, if you want, to prepare a proposal.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal basis:</strong> steps taken at your request before a possible contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR), and our
      legitimate interest in answering business enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How:</strong> the inquiry is stored in a database run by Cloudflare and sent by email (through Resend) to
      us and, as a confirmation, to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> inquiries are deleted automatically after 24 months. If we start working together,
      the relevant details become part of our client records.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="waitlists">Game waitlists</h2>
  <p>
    When you join the waitlist for one of our <a href="/games">games</a>, we receive your email address, the game, the
    platform you chose and the time you signed up.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Why:</strong> to send you one email when that game launches. No newsletter, and nothing else.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw it any time by emailing us.</li>
    <li><strong>How:</strong> the entry is stored in a database run by Cloudflare.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> until the launch email has been sent, and in any case no longer than 24 months. Anyone
      under 16 needs a parent or guardian to sign up for them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The games on this site run in your browser. Nothing about how you play is sent to us.</p>

  <h2 id="email">Email</h2>
  <p>
    Messages sent to {site.email} are forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to our mailbox, which is hosted by Google
    (Gmail). We keep correspondence for as long as needed to deal with your request, and no longer than 24 months unless
    we work together.
  </p>

  <h2 id="spam">Spam protection</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from bots. On that page only, Turnstile processes technical
    information about your browser and device. It is not used for advertising. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest
    in keeping the form free of abuse (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Umami Cloud to count visits and a few events (for example, a click on "Start a project" or a submitted
    inquiry). Umami does not use cookies and does not collect personal data; we only see aggregated numbers. We never send
    your name, email or messages to analytics. If your browser sends a "Do Not Track" signal, no analytics are recorded.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and logs</h2>
  <p>
    The website is hosted on Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site from attacks, Cloudflare processes
    technical data such as your IP address and browser information. This is our legitimate interest in running a secure
    website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2 id="booking">Booking a call</h2>
  <p>
    After an inquiry we offer a link to book a call on Cal.com. The booking page is not embedded in our site: it only
    loads if you open it. What you enter there is processed by Cal.com under its own privacy policy, and shared with us
    to arrange the call.
  </p>

  <h2 id="processors">Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, database, spam protection (Turnstile) and email forwarding.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sending inquiry notifications and confirmations.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>: our email inbox (Gmail).</li>
    <li><strong>Umami</strong>: cookieless, aggregated website analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>Cal.com</strong>: booking calls, only if you choose to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers process data outside the EU and EEA, including in the United States. Where they do, they rely
    on transfer safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses, as described in their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not set cookies, so there is no cookie banner. Cloudflare Turnstile on the contact page may store
    technical data needed for spam protection, as described in Cloudflare's privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for access to the personal data we hold about you, and ask us to correct it, delete it, restrict its
    use, or give it to you in a portable format. You can also object to processing based on legitimate interest. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply within a month.
  </p>
  <p>You also have the right to complain to a data protection supervisory authority.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change how we handle data, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</LegalLayout>
